            <ArticleTitle>Bayes' theorem--a review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>319-28</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Formal probability analysis based on Bayes' theorem greatly enhances the diagnostic capabilities of exercise testing in the detection of coronary artery disease. The pretest characteristics of a patient must be considered along with the test results in arriving at a post-test probability of disease. The essential concepts of probability analysis have broad applications in the entire field of medicine.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
